{
  "app": "c64-visual-assembler",
  "d64": {
    "diskName": "EXOMCDEMO",
    "extras": [
      {
        "crunch": true,
        "decompressAddress": "",
        "loadAddress": "2000",
        "name": "MULTI-COLOR",
        "sourcePath": "multi-color.bin"
      }
    ],
    "progName": "EXOMCDEMO"
  },
  "expertText": "* = $0801\n; EXO Multicolor Demo — LOADFILE compressed bitmap to $C000, EXODECRUNCH decompresses to $2000, then displays it.\n; Run via D64 setup: MULTI-COLOR is pre-configured (Addr=C000, Dst=2000, EXO=on). VA compresses multi-color.bin with exomizer mem backward mode, target $2000, loads to $C000.\n; After LOADFILE, KERNAL sets ZP $AE/$AF to end-of-load. EXODECRUNCH copies those to ZP $04/$05 (depacker source-end pointer), then JSRs depacker at $B000 which decompresses backward to $2000.\n\n.include \"img-macros\"\n    SEI\n    LDA #$00\n    STA $D020\n    STA $D021\n    JSR $E544\n.text 10, 12, \"loading multi-color...   \"\n.loadfile \"MULTI-COLOR\", 8, failtramp\n    JMP loadok\nfailtramp:\n    JMP loaderr\nloadok:\n.exodecrunch depacker=$B000\n    LDA #$00\n    STA $D020\n.invoke Copy\n; Screen and color data copied. Bitmap $2000, screen $0400, color $D800. Set up VIC-II for multicolor bitmap.\n    LDA #$18\n    STA $D018\n    LDA #$3B\n    STA $D011\n    LDA #$18\n    STA $D016\nmain:\n    JMP main\nloaderr:\n.text 10, 12, \"load error - attach d64!  \"\nhalt:\n    JMP halt\n* = $B000\n; Exomizer 3 raw depacker — compile decrunch.asm from the Exomizer distribution and save as exo-decrunch.bin next to this project. ZP usage: $FB-$FC (src pointer).\n.incbin \"exo-decrunch.bin\", $B000",
